Read the following passage and answer the question that follows.

Aniline is dissolved in dilute hydrochloric acid, the solution is cooled to 273–278 K, and aqueous sodium nitrite is added slowly. Benzenediazonium chloride (D) is formed.

C₆H₅NH₂ + NaNO₂ + 2HCl → C₆H₅N₂⁺Cl⁻ + NaCl + 2H₂O

Separate portions of the cold solution of D are then used as follows:
(i) treated with CuCl/HCl;
(ii) treated with aqueous KI;
(iii) treated with fluoroboric acid (HBF₄), and the precipitate is heated;
(iv) treated with aniline;
(v) treated with hypophosphorous acid (H₃PO₂).

